WEBVTT

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.020
Coming back here feels so relaxing...

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.040
It already has that feeling of being "home."

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.610
I agree.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.990
Come on, guys. Shouldn't you 
at least take your gear off?

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:18.450
Yeah. We should.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.190
Okay. Let's do that.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.700
Yes, let's.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.500
Huh? I can't move.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.510
Could someone have cast paralysis magic on us?

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.260
That's not it. We're all just exhausted.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:39.570
Now that you mention it, all we've done since 
graduating is take on one quest after another.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.600
We never really rested, did we?

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.930
An abusive corporation...

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.520
What does that mean?

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.740
A company that crushes workers 
under impossible workloads,

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.330
squeezing out every drop in search of profit.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:52.680
A villainous employer.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.030
That brings shame on merchants everywhere!

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.370
Stare...

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.680
Huh? Wait! When did I become your employer?

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.000
I'm your friend, right?

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.120
And I'm just as tired as you are!

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.120
Oh! You see this type a lot 
with macho-style employers!

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.830
They say that since they're tired too,

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:12.400
everyone should work even harder,
 and they push for more.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.380
Honestly! Did I say anything like that?

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.730
Then, what do we think of taking 
a little break starting tomorrow?

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:20.430
We've managed to save up quite a bit already.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.080
What? Really?

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.600
Huh. Reina-san is the 
happiest out of everyone.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.060
How long are you going to force 
this "employer" role on me?

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.440
Right! Starting tomorrow, we're on vacation!

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.000
Yay!

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.300
I have something I wanted to do!

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.400
So do I!

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:39.030
I'm going to start by sleeping in,
so please don't wake me.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.550
And I... I wonder what I'll do.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.000
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.010
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.010
<b>Didn't I Say We Should Take Breaks Sometimes?!</b>

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.560
Good morning, Mile-chan.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.460
Morning, Pauline-san.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.530
Where are Reina-san and Mavis-san?

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.150
They've been up and about for a while now.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.720
Didn't Mavis-san say she was sleeping in?

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.730
She did, but it seems she woke up 
and went out earlier than anyone else.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.160
When I woke up, she was already gone.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:55.410
Reina and I had breakfast together,
 then she went out.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:59.280
So that means I slept in the longest.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.680
We're on vacation, so you 
shouldn't let it trouble you.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.330
Pauline-san, what are you writing?

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.430
This is the Crimson Vow's accounts ledger.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.290
All of our income and expenses 
since our founding.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.770
I've been wanting to organize 
it all for a while now.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:19.820
Wait... Does that mean you remember all 
of what we earned and spent so far?

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:24.070
I never forget anything when it comes to money.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.580
<i>Is it her merchant's blood?!</i>

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.160
<i>Pauline-san is terrifying!</i>

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:33.410
Oh, right. Both Reina-san and Mavis-san 
said they had things they wanted to do.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.400
I wonder what they're doing.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.850
Reina wouldn't tell me,

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.920
but Mavis said she was going to a nearby café.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.360
Café?

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.880
Mavis-san is...

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:50.910
I see her.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:51.560
Huh?

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.200
That's amazing!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.290
Just that one spot has this 
super-elevated atmosphere!

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.390
Just what you'd expect from
someone of noble birth.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:15.790
She must have spent her free time like 
that since she was a little girl.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.470
Say, isn't that person over there just sublime?

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:21.580
Yes! But are they a man? A woman?

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.300
Either way works just fine!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.890
Mavis-san!

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.820
Oh, Mile, Pauline! You came here.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:31.480
Mavis-san, you really look 
like a noble! You're so cool!

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:32.890
R-Really?

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:36.500
You wouldn't happen to have a childhood 
friend named André, would you?

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.060
Um, no, I don't.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.650
What about a best friend 
named Marie who's a princess?

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:44.080
One who says things like, "As long as 
I've got cake, I can do anything!"

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.530
I don't know anyone who says things like that.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.460
That's a shame.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:49.320
What's a shame?

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.080
Reina isn't with you?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.140
She went out before us.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:57.320
No matter how many times I asked, 
she wouldn't tell me where she was going.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.080
Why not? That's stand-offish of her.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:04.800
Reina-san just went through something that 
made her basically relive her painful past.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.300
Maybe she wanted to be alone.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.160
That could be.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.300
She is a sensitive person, after all.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:18.810
It's gotta be this one!

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.060
Oh, but this one's nice, too.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.760
But I think...

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:28.680
I can't let those three know 
I enjoy doing things like this.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:32.520
Tee-hee! Reina-san, you're so 
much girlier than I thought!

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:38.960
Reina! I've written to my father,
asking him to send frilly dresses for you!

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:43.540
Reina, perhaps you should switch 
jobs from "mage" to "princess."

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.260
I can just hear them poking fun at me.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.970
Mile-san and Mavis-san might be like that,

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:52.320
but I don't think Pauline-san 
would ever say those things.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.800
You think so?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.120
Reina-san! I would love for you 
to serve customers wearing that!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.980
Huh? Serve customers?

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.430
Lenny?

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.420
Wh-Why are you here?

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:06.840
I came out to shop for a few 
things we were running low on,

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.570
and came across something very interesting.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.800
To think I'd see the most stoic 
member of the Crimson Vow

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.320
shopping for accessories of all things!

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:16.760
I'm done for.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.760
Starting tomorrow, my name will go from

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:22.320
"Crimson Reina" to "Reina the 
Pretending-to-Be-Sullen."

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:25.520
Why do you think I'd go and tell everyone?

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:27.460
Huh? You're not going to?

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.520
Huh?

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:33.220
The thing is, I like those kinds 
of accessories too, but...

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:36.880
I'm not confident in my fashion sense, so...

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:40.920
Just leave it to your big sister here.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.190
Really?

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:46.560
Mavis-san really is a noble, isn't she?

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:49.280
I mean, the book she was reading 
was a poetry collection.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.040
It's those kinds of things 
that show your upbringing.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:54.900
You say that, but you're a noble too,
 aren't you, Mile-chan?

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:55.550
Huh?

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:58.240
Oh. Well, yes, but...

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:01.710
For me, things are a little complicated...
Sort of a special case...

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:03.550
<i>After all, my past life as a commoner</i>

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.630
<i>lasted longer than my 
current one as a noble has.</i>

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:10.680
That's right. You mentioned 
that your family shunned you.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:14.200
You weren't allowed to 
live as a noble, were you?

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.230
I'm so sorry for asking you 
about something so uncomfortable.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:20.080
Huh? Oh, uh, not at all. It's fine.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.200
<i>She misunderstood in a convenient way,</i>

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.020
<i>so I'll just pretend it's that.</i>

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.120
Locked in a dank, underground cell,
 in tattered clothes...

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:30.900
Not even given a decent meal...

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:31.900
Huh?

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.150
And once you escaped the underground prison,

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:39.540
you became wealthy, so you could exact 
revenge upon those who had wronged you!

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.410
So that I can...

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:44.460
<i>I think that </i>Altered Folktale<i> I told before,</i>

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:47.920
<i>"Monte, Chris, and Count," 
is getting mixed in here.</i>

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.400
So...

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.680
Pauline-san, you're going to keep 
working on the accounts ledger, right?

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:55.160
Oh, yes. That's what I was planning.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:57.300
In that case, I'll go out, too.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:02.220
And having said that, 
there's nothing for me to do.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:06.400
But when it comes to spending 
time on my own, I'm a pro!

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.500
After all, in the eighteen 
years of my last life,

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.380
I didn't ever really have any friends!

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.700
Why are you stating such a tragic 
fact as though you're proud of it?

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:16.710
No, no...

00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:20.790
After nearly twenty years of it,
 it really wasn't that bad.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.700
I think that, in itself, is very sad.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.770
Now, let's see. What should I do? First...

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.340
Is something wrong?

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:33.860
Huh? I can't think of anything.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:34.500
What?

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:38.030
That's weird. What did I used to do?

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:40.160
Oh! I watched TV and stuff.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.510
We don't have that in this world.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:47.500
True. And there's no internet or 
game consoles... No manga, either.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.060
Got it!

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.480
Leap!

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:56.990
That's not quite it.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:57.960
Hup!

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.240
Mile-sama, what are you doing?

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:06.710
It came to me a while ago, and I've been 
thinking I'd practice when I had the time.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.790
It's sure to come in handy.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.580
The jumping dogeza!

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.170
Jump!

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:20.390
Nailed it! I am now ready to 
use this move at any moment!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:25.650
I have no idea as to when or where 
you might need to use that move,

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:27.930
but I am glad you're satisfied.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:30.700
Now, has it been about an hour?

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:32.880
It hasn't even been ten minutes yet.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:34.290
What? Really?

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.530
Then what should I do next?

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.640
It really is strange.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:45.540
I used to be able to think of 
things to do on my own right away.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:48.100
No, no. Let's calm down here.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:53.040
I should be able to kill a day or 
two of this vacation, no problem!

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.030
Is it really something to fret over?

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:58.550
Well, this used to be the thing I was best at.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:01.910
Without this, I won't have 
any redeeming features left.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.270
Your self-esteem really 
is at rock bottom, isn't it?

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:10.560
I'll just carve a random Nendonaroid 
and draw some meaningless doodles.

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:13.950
I'll read through some random 
papers I found near the trash.

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.720
I'll lie around and daydream up a story.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.040
Then I'll start wanting to just laze around.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.480
All of those things seem 
rather pointless to me.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:23.440
That's all right.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:27.990
If the Nendonaroid sells, or they enjoy 
my <i>Altered Folktale</i>, that's great,

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:32.240
but I'm fundamentally bad at trying to 
be of use or make something of my own.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:35.350
Doing something pointless lets 
you just relax and do it, right?

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:37.920
You're really just killing time, aren't you?

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.290
Exactly.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.260
All right...

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.550
Oh, there she is!

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:43.930
Huh? You're all together?

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.270
The others came back,

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:49.600
so we thought we'd come invite you
 to do something together with us.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:50.430
Huh?

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.950
So could you hurry up and wrap 
up whatever it is you're doing?

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:57.490
Huh? You have sand in your bangs.
 What were you doing?

00:11:57.490 --> 00:12:00.990
Oh! This? I was sort of working 
on a secret technique.

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:04.620
Huh? You don't want to finish?

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:05.530
It's all right.

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.960
In that case, let's head back to the room.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:10.390
Sorry. This is all because of Reina.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:12.020
What are you talking about?

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:15.280
You're the one who wouldn't 
quit saying how bored you were!

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:15.920
Honestly.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:17.250
Is that so?

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:21.420
<i>So that's what it was...</i>

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:24.670
<i>I started getting bad at being on my own...</i>

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:28.120
<i>when I started spending more time with them.</i>

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.650
Say! Should we all hang 
out together again today?

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:36.620
Sounds good!

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:37.690
Yes, it does!

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:38.820
What about you, Mile?

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.150
Of course!

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:42.400
Then since we hung out in our room yesterday,

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.550
today we'll go out somewhere!

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.260
What?

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:46.500
Is something wrong?

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:47.990
Do you not want to go out?

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.210
It's not that.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.530
It's just been a while since 
I went anywhere with friends.

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:54.250
I got a little emotional.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.410
I see.

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:58.880
If that's the case, then we should 
go out together a lot more!

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:03.150
Then why don't we have Mile 
decide where we're going?

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:03.590
Huh?

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.800
Yes, let's do that.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.590
I'm in favor. We'll go anywhere with you.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:08.900
What do you want to do?

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:11.600
Um. Let's see...

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:13.680
I want to go sea bathing!

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:16.840
Sea bathing? What's that?

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:20.560
Maybe she means going to the 
seaside and playing in the water?

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:21.940
Yes! That's it!

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:26.150
But I've never gone sea bathing before.

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:27.330
Me neither.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.020
Me neither. I've only heard of it.

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:33.290
Don't worry! I'll get everything ready!

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:36.290
Well, if Mile says she wants to...

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:41.110
It has been hotter recently. 
It might feel nice to go the beach.

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:42.000
That's true.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:44.850
Then, could we go tomorrow?

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:46.490
Huh? Why?

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.600
I want to get everything we need ready.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:49.970
First, we need swimsuits!

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:51.100
Swimsuits?

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.340
Special clothes for playing in the water.

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:55.180
If you go in the water in normal clothes,

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:57.440
they'll get soaked and heavy,
 and stick to you.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.600
In a worst case scenario,
 they could become see-through.

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:00.560
I see.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:03.920
You wear swimsuits right against your skin,

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:06.810
so you need to know your exact size.

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:07.920
Which is why...

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.600
I hope you'll allow me to measure you.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.180
Naked!

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:12.080
What?

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:17.400
Do I really have to be naked?

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:20.100
It's something that has to 
stand up to waves and swimming.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:23.920
If it doesn't fit right, 
it could slip and come off.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.490
Fine...

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.100
Huh? Wait! Why are you touching me there?

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.990
It's just the measuring tape.

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:32.360
You know, it's hard to tell 
through your clothes,

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:35.240
but your curves are quite 
soft and have a lovely shape.

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.880
Don't stare at me like that!

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:41.510
It really is embarrassing for 
someone to see you naked, isn't it?

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:42.340
Is it?

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:42.880
Huh?

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.400
You don't mind it?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:48.720
Since I was little, I've always had maids to 
help when I was bathing or changing clothes.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.340
That's a noble for you!

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:53.480
Reina-san, your bottom 
is all pink and adorable.

00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:56.210
Color has nothing to do 
with measuring, does it?

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:06.370
Next, Pauline-san! Please come in!

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:07.920
Oh! Coming!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.300
Be careful.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.050
Huh? Of what?

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:12.720
Pauline-san!

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:20.440
Now, then. I'll go buy materials for 
the swimsuits, plus other things we'll need.

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:22.840
She's really going all out, isn't she?

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:25.380
Is sea bathing really that much fun?

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:29.680
The kind I know about, you just 
spend a leisurely time at the beach.

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.280
Why sea bathing?

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.580
If we're all going to do something together,

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:40.540
I want it to be something I 
didn't get to do my last life.

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:47.710
There it is!

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.170
The ocean!

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:53.840
We're here!

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.670
It's like we reserved it for ourselves!

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:57.590
It was worth waking up early.

00:15:57.590 --> 00:15:59.560
Now, at long last!

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.560
These are the things we need for sea bathing!

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:05.360
Did you make all of these?

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:08.880
No one sold anything like 
what I had in my country.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.020
So I recreated them using substitutes!

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:12.080
That's amazing.

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:13.600
What do you do with them?

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:16.240
With this one, you bob.
With this one, you squeal.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:19.050
With this one, you exchange shots.
With this one, you stab.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:20.410
This one, you lie on.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.290
This one, you put on.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:24.170
I have no idea what she just said.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:26.000
She seems sort of frenzied.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.960
I think I'm going to mess up the order...

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:28.460
Not at all!

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:32.790
There isn't an order, and you don't 
have to do everything at once.

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:33.550
And now...

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:35.430
These are your swimsuits!

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.310
This is the whole thing?

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.890
I feel like there isn't enough fabric.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:42.320
Don't worry!

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:43.580
But this is...

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:44.560
It's a little...

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:48.150
Please, I'm begging you! Swimsuits are 
the crowning glory of sea bathing!

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.970
There can be no sea bathing 
without swimsuits!

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:52.070
Please wear them!

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:53.900
Jump!

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:55.570
I beg of you!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:56.730
Wait, Mile...

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:58.620
You don't have to go that far.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:00.480
You'll wear them?

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.870
So that's what you were doing out back.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:07.000
Well, we did say we'd go along 
with whatever you wanted.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.250
Then, without delay...

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.880
Changing rooms!

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:12.490
She really is prepared.

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:14.880
Huh? Why isn't there a room for you, Mile?

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:17.010
Why, thank you for asking.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:19.350
As per the basics, I am fully prepared...

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.220
I came wearing it under my clothes!

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:27.440
Now, all of you change, too!

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.110
Now, when I call your name, please come out!

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.920
First, we have Mavis-san!

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:42.070
Just what I'd expect from 
you, Mavis-san. It's perfect!

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:43.330
I-Is it?

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.730
And moving on, we have Pauline-san!

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:51.960
Pauline-san! That's an out!

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.960
Am I wearing it wrong?

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.990
No. You're fine.

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:58.210
I do think these clothes are cute,

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:01.190
but I still feel like there 
isn't nearly enough fabric.

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:04.640
Not at all! In my country, 
everyone wears these.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:07.280
They bring out a woman's charms 
to their maximum level!

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:08.730
They're magic clothes!

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:10.760
Next, we have Reina-san!

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:16.280
What is with this wig?

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:17.570
Honestly, Mile!

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:20.240
Reina-san, it really suits you.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.700
Y-You think so?

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:22.580
Huh?

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:26.650
Wha? Huh? Y-Y-Your bust is—

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:27.460
Huh?

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:30.820
Oh, Mile, did your bust get bigger?

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:32.700
Yes, I thought you were fla—

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:35.090
...more modestly sized, weren't you?

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:37.390
Mile! What is the meaning of this?

00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:39.530
It's because I'm still growing.

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:42.380
<i>Actually, my top is the only one</i>

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:44.410
<i>that I put padding in.</i>

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.470
Just what I'd expect from you, Mile-sama.
 That's playing dirty.

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:50.230
One, two, three, four,

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:53.480
five, six, seven, eight.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.480
All right. That's our warm-up exercises done.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:57.520
Okay!

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:59.810
This is the first time I've 
ever swum in the ocean!

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:01.130
Me, too!

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:03.120
Oh! Wait a moment!

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.160
What is it?

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:06.760
There's a particular etiquette 
to going into the ocean.

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:08.750
We have to follow the rules.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:09.530
Huh?

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:11.510
There's an etiquette to it?

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:15.150
That's right! You can't just go swim.

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:16.820
We can't swim?

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.600
If you immerse yourself in the water,

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:21.760
no one can see the cute swimsuit 
you took such pains to wear.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.800
Aren't these swimsuits meant for swimming?

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:24.780
No, they aren't.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:27.880
They are simply costumes used 
to enliven the beach atmosphere.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:31.680
But yesterday you talked about 
functionality and drag, didn't you?

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:33.660
That was only if the worst happened.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:36.900
So for sea bathing,
 actual swimming is the worst.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:42.990
Girls usually use those things I made to 
lie back and relax, or they play in the sand.

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:47.830
They don't swim! They frolic in 
the shallows, giggling and squealing!

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.460
Somehow, this is very different 
from what I'd imagined.

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:53.540
Now! Start the giggling and squealing!

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:35.540
Sea bathing certainly is fun.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:37.040
Quite a lot of fun.

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:40.510
Not bad at all. It might be fun to
 come here every once in a while.

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:43.530
I'm so glad! I had fun, too!

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:48.470
What are you girls doing?

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:51.720
Oh, it's called sea bathing.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:53.620
Sea bathing, huh?

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:57.480
And you do it like that, nearly naked,
 even though you're girls?

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:02.140
Wait! Mile! You said this 
was normal, didn't you?

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:05.300
It's normal in m-my country...

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:08.620
Wow! Naked girls! Naked girls!

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:09.660
Don't look!

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.250
K—

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:15.710
K?

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.500
Kyaa!

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:23.330
Honestly! That disaster was all your fault!

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:27.730
As per the basics, I was completely unprepared,
 and forgot to bring a change of underwear.

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:29.500
It's all breezy under my clothes.

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:30.640
Stop talking!

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:33.850
Now, now. Mile didn't mean any harm.

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:36.120
I really didn't know!

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:40.610
I never thought that swimsuits in this 
worl—country would cover up so much!

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:43.610
What kind of country did you used to live in?

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:45.610
It does seem a little strange.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:50.780
No, it wasn't! It's a 
really nice worl—country!

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:52.000
It really is!

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:53.870
All right, we understand.

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:58.980
Anyway! I think that a penalty of no 
allowance for three months sounds about right.

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:00.210
What?

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:01.740
Right, Pauline?

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:02.830
Huh?

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:08.660
Pauline-san?

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:12.970
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!
